# Line endings, fixed by policy rather than by each machine's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# Why this file exists: `core.autocrlf=true` (the default on Windows) rewrites every
# text file to CRLF on checkout. `tools/build-knowledge.mjs` strips YAML frontmatter
# by testing `startsWith("---\n")`, which is false for `---\r\n` — so on Windows the
# frontmatter block was being spliced into the persona prompt instead of removed,
# and nothing noticed because the check that catches it only ran against a `data/`
# tree built on a machine with LF. The parser now normalises CRLF itself (so it is
# correct regardless of how the tree was produced), and this file stops the churn at
# the source.

# Normalise everything to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Windows-only scripting that genuinely needs CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
